19
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:38,238
♪♪♪

20
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:16,009
♪♪♪

21
00:01:16,009 --> 00:01:17,043
Tyra: MA, THERE'S A GIRL

22
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:19,446
THAT, UM, WE ELIMINATED
LAST NIGHT.

23
00:01:19,446 --> 00:01:20,480
HER NAME IS CASSIE.

24
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:23,550
IT WAS BETWEEN CASSIE
AND TOCCARA,

25
00:01:23,550 --> 00:01:25,452
WHO'S LIKE
A FULL-FIGURED GIRL.

26
00:01:25,452 --> 00:01:26,920
THE JUDGES WERE, LIKE,
GOING BACK AND FORTH.

27
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,955
IT WAS REALLY, REALLY CRAZY,
BUT IN THE END,

28
00:01:28,955 --> 00:01:32,158
CASSIE WAS VOTED
TO GO HOME.

29
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:34,894
AND IT'S KIND OF HARD FOR ME

30
00:01:34,894 --> 00:01:37,631
BECAUSE SHE CONFESSED
TO ME THAT SHE'S BULIMIC.

31
00:01:37,631 --> 00:01:38,765
Carolyn: HMM.

32
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:40,367
Tyra: AND I TRIED
TO GET HER HELP...

33
00:01:40,367 --> 00:01:43,336
Cassie: YOU CAN TELL ME I
SHOULDN'T DO THAT ALL YOU WANT,

34
00:01:43,336 --> 00:01:45,238
BUT IF I FEEL LIKE
I'M STILL GONNA DO IT,

35
00:01:45,238 --> 00:01:46,473
I'M NEVER GONNA BE HELPED.

36
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:48,341
Tyra: AND SHE WAS, LIKE,
"I DON'T LIKE THERAPISTS,

37
00:01:48,341 --> 00:01:51,344
I DON'T WANT TO GO, AND I'M
NOT GONNA STOP DOING THIS,

38
00:01:51,344 --> 00:01:52,412
SO IT DOESN'T MATTER."

39
00:01:52,412 --> 00:01:54,281
AND I JUST FEEL LIKE,
YOU KNOW,

40
00:01:54,281 --> 00:01:55,915
LIKE, WHAT ELSE CAN I DO?

41
00:01:55,915 --> 00:01:57,884
Carolyn: IT'S NOT LIKE
YOU THREW HER AWAY, TYRA.

42
00:01:57,884 --> 00:01:59,419
YOU CAN ONLY DO SO MUCH

43
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:03,490
TO HELP A PERSON
THAT IS BASICALLY LOST.

44
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:05,292
SHE HAS TO FIND HERSELF.

45
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:07,360
SHE NEEDS TO DO
SOME SOUL-SEARCHING.

46
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:10,697
SHE NEEDS TO LOOK WITHIN

47
00:02:10,697 --> 00:02:13,466
TO FIND THE STRENGTH
TO GET THE HELP THAT SHE NEEDS.

48
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:14,934
Tyra: RIGHT.

49
00:02:14,934 --> 00:02:16,870
Carolyn: SO IT'S OKAY.

50
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:25,378
♪♪♪

51
00:02:25,378 --> 00:02:26,379
Toccara: LAST ELIMINATION,

52
00:02:26,379 --> 00:02:27,781
SOMEONE ON THE PANEL
SAYS...

53
00:02:27,781 --> 00:02:30,350
Nolé: AMERICA IS NOT READY
TO SEE A PLUS-SIZED TOP MODEL.

54
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:32,952
Toccara:
I'M LIKE, "WHOA." PFFT.

55
00:02:32,952 --> 00:02:35,822
MY MISSION HERE
IS TO BREAK THE NORM

56
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:38,391
AND LET YOU KNOW THAT BIG GIRLS
CAN DO HIGH FASHION, TOO.

57
00:02:38,391 --> 00:02:39,459
Eva:
YOU KNOW HOW FATTENING

58
00:02:39,459 --> 00:02:41,094
THESE BEAN AND CHEESE
BURRITOS ARE?

59
00:02:41,094 --> 00:02:42,562
- Yaya: NO.
- Ann: WHOSE IS THIS?

60
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:44,331
Eva: IT'S FOR YOU. GO AHEAD.
PUT SOME CHEESE ON THAT.

61
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:46,499
(Spanish accent)
AND DON'T BE STINGY, OKAY?

62
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:48,368
Ann: OH, STOP IT,
NOT TODAY, PLEASE.

63
00:02:48,368 --> 00:02:50,704
Eva: A LOT OF THE OTHER GIRLS
SEE ME AS LOUD AND CRAZY.

64
00:02:50,704 --> 00:02:52,972
BUT I HAVE FEELINGS.
I HAVE EMOTIONS. I HAVE LAYERS.

65
00:02:52,972 --> 00:02:55,108
LIKE, ONE PERSON ISN'T
THE SAME ALL THE TIME.

66
00:02:55,108 --> 00:02:58,378
BUT THIS IS A COMPETITION,
AND SO ALL MY GUARDS ARE UP.

67
00:02:58,378 --> 00:03:00,413
Ann: THESE ARE ACTUALLY
SURPRISINGLY GOOD FOR YOU.

68
00:03:00,413 --> 00:03:02,449
LIKE, THERE'S HARDLY
ANY CARBOHYDRATES IN THESE.

69
00:03:02,449 --> 00:03:04,751
Yaya: CARBOHYDRATES,
SCHMARBOHYDRATES.

70
00:03:04,751 --> 00:03:06,619
I DEFINITELY COME
FROM A DIFFERENT PLACE

71
00:03:06,619 --> 00:03:09,255
THAN OTHER PEOPLE
IN THE HOUSE.

72
00:03:09,255 --> 00:03:10,323
Ann: (belches)

73
00:03:10,323 --> 00:03:11,558
Yaya: I'M NOT
JUST GETTING SWEPT UP

74
00:03:11,558 --> 00:03:13,526
IN THIS SUPERFICIAL
WORLD.

75
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:17,097
DO YOU EVER THINK THAT
THIS LOW CARB FASCINATION

76
00:03:17,097 --> 00:03:20,066
IS A GIMMICK?

77
00:03:20,066 --> 00:03:22,635
Ann: YAYA HAS HER LITTLE
BITCHY, LIKE, ATTITUDE.

78
00:03:22,635 --> 00:03:24,237
SHE THINKS
SHE KNOWS EVERYTHING.

79
00:03:24,237 --> 00:03:25,739
Yaya: LOOK, SERIOUSLY,

80
00:03:25,739 --> 00:03:29,209
ALL THIS TALK ABOUT LOW CARB
THINGS IS REALLY ANNOYING.

81
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,477
(knock on door)

82
00:03:30,477 --> 00:03:32,712
Ann: I WAS THE FIRST ONE
TO HEAR A KNOCK ON THE DOOR.

83
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:34,280
Woman: HI, HOW ARE YOU?

84
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,448
Ann:
I'M GOOD. HOW ARE YOU?

85
00:03:35,448 --> 00:03:36,850
Woman: GOOD, THANK YOU.

86
00:03:36,850 --> 00:03:37,951
Ann: AND I'M LIKE,
"AM I SUPPOSED TO KNOW

87
00:03:37,951 --> 00:03:39,052
WHO THESE PEOPLE ARE?"

88
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:40,854
Rebecca: MY NAME IS
REBECCA WEINBERG.

89
00:03:40,854 --> 00:03:43,490
I'M A STYLIST--
AN EMMY AWARD-WINNING STYLIST.

90
00:03:43,490 --> 00:03:45,191
Paul:
AND I'M PAUL WILMOT,

91
00:03:45,191 --> 00:03:47,360
AND WE HAVE A PUBLIC RELATIONS
COMPANY IN NEW YORK

92
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,095
CALLED PAUL WILMOT
COMMUNICATIONS.

93
00:03:49,095 --> 00:03:50,897
I'M WITH MY COLLEAGUE
HAMPTON CARNEY TODAY.

94
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:52,499
WHAT WE'D LIKE TO DO IS
WE'D LIKE TO GIVE YOU

95
00:03:52,499 --> 00:03:55,001
A BIT OF A TUTORIAL
TODAY ABOUT IMAGE.

96
00:03:55,001 --> 00:03:57,003
WE'RE GONNA GIVE YOU SOME TIPS
ON EVENTS AND SO ON.

97
00:03:57,003 --> 00:03:58,938
AND THE SAME TIME YOU'RE
GONNA HAVE THE OPPORTUNITY

98
00:03:58,938 --> 00:04:00,206
TO SIT WITH REBECCA,

99
00:04:00,206 --> 00:04:01,408
AND SHE'S GONNA GO
THROUGH A CLOSET WITH YOU

100
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:02,742
AND REALLY HELP YOU
CREATE YOUR LOOK.

101
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:04,344
AND SHE'LL MAKE
SOME SUGGESTIONS.

102
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:06,346
HAMPTON AND I ARE GONNA
START WITH YAYA.

103
00:04:06,346 --> 00:04:08,081
Rebecca: AND I'M GONNA
TAKE AMANDA.

104
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:10,049
Hampton: COOL.

105
00:04:10,049 --> 00:04:12,752
Yaya: I AM A VERY WORLDLY
INDIVIDUAL.

106
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:15,688
I JUST GRADUATED FROM
AN IVY LEAGUE UNIVERSITY,

107
00:04:15,688 --> 00:04:17,490
AND I FEEL LIKE I CAN
TALK TO PEOPLE

108
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:18,825
ABOUT ALMOST ANYTHING.

109
00:04:18,825 --> 00:04:20,860
I'M JUST NOT SURE WHAT KIND
OF CONVERSATION

110
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,495
IS APPROPRIATE
IN THIS WORLD.

111
00:04:22,495 --> 00:04:26,032
Hampton: NEVER THINK THAT
YOU KNOW ALL THE ANSWERS.

112
00:04:26,032 --> 00:04:27,267
'CAUSE PEOPLE
WILL LIKE YOU BETTER.

113
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,669
AND I THINK YOU CAN TAKE IT
REALLY FAR THAT WAY.

114
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:31,538
Rebecca: PICK OUT
YOUR FAVORITE FIVE THINGS.

115
00:04:31,538 --> 00:04:34,140
I JUST KINDA WANNA GET
AN IDEA OF WHO YOU ARE.

116
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:35,141
Amanda: MM-HMM.

117
00:04:35,141 --> 00:04:36,509
Rebecca:
YOU KNOW, I HAVE TO SAY

118
00:04:36,509 --> 00:04:39,012
WHEN I LOOK AT THESE THINGS,
THEY LOOK A LITTLE CHEAP.

119
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:41,781
Amanda: I'M VERY POOR.

120
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:43,917
Rebecca: ALL RIGHT, BUT
THE IDEA IS TO TAKE SOMETHING

121
00:04:43,917 --> 00:04:46,519
THAT'S INEXPENSIVE AND KIND OF,
LIKE, TWIST IT

122
00:04:46,519 --> 00:04:48,488
AND MAKE IT LOOK
MORE THAN IT IS.

123
00:04:48,488 --> 00:04:49,956
Eva:
WHY AM I EVA THE DIVA?

124
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:51,224
Paul: YOU LOVE IT.

125
00:04:51,224 --> 00:04:53,660
Eva: EVERYBODY FREAKIN'
SAYS TO ME THAT I AM A DIVA.

126
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:56,329
SO HOW DO I NOT BE A DIVA?

127
00:04:56,329 --> 00:04:57,330
Paul:
HOW DO YOU DO THAT?

128
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:58,932
BY SHOWING THE BEST
POSSIBLE MANNERS

129
00:04:58,932 --> 00:05:00,867
TO PROVE THAT UNDERNEATH
ALL THAT IS A REALLY--

130
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:04,003
A VERY GOLDEN PERSON,
A VERY NICE PERSON.

131
00:05:04,003 --> 00:05:05,705
Rebecca:
VERY EARTH MOTHER.

132
00:05:05,705 --> 00:05:07,340
Yaya: I WOULDN'T MIND
STICKING TO THAT STYLE.

133
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,441
Rebecca: THAT STYLE?

134
00:05:08,441 --> 00:05:10,877
BUT IT'S FINE TO STICK
TO A STYLE.

135
00:05:10,877 --> 00:05:13,913
BUT IT'S ALSO--IT'S LIKE,
IF YOU GO TO A TOOTHPASTE AD,

136
00:05:13,913 --> 00:05:16,182
ARE YOU GONNA GO
IN A DASHIKI?

137
00:05:16,182 --> 00:05:19,519
OR ARE YOU GONNA, LIKE,
GO IN A T-SHIRT AND JEANS?

138
00:05:19,519 --> 00:05:20,687
Yaya: IN ORDER
TO BE SUCCESSFUL,

139
00:05:20,687 --> 00:05:23,189
I DON'T HAVE TO CONFORM
TO THESE CONSTRAINTS.

140
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:24,324
Rebecca: STEREOTYPES.

141
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:26,426
I SEE THIS IN GENERAL,
BUT WHEN I SEE YOU

142
00:05:26,426 --> 00:05:29,229
PULL OUT THOSE KINDS
OF THINGS, I SEE NO VARIETY.

143
00:05:29,229 --> 00:05:30,797
MIX IT UP A LITTLE BIT.

144
00:05:30,797 --> 00:05:32,832
MAYBE BY ADDING
A LITTLE COLOR?

145
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:35,802
IT'S LIKE,
"I'M THE HAPPY YAYA."

146
00:05:35,802 --> 00:05:37,103
Paul: TELL ME ABOUT YOU.

147
00:05:37,103 --> 00:05:40,840
Ann: I'M NOT THE MOST PROPER
ET CETERA, ET CETERA.

148
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,141
Hampton: EVEN IF YOU'RE
GONNA SAY SOMETHING

149
00:05:42,141 --> 00:05:44,878
THAT MAY BE NAUGHTY OR
SOMETHING, SAY IT INTELLIGENTLY.

150
00:05:44,878 --> 00:05:47,480
Rebecca: I SEE A LOT OF, LIKE,
TRENDY STUFF GOING ON HERE.

151
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,082
SO IT'S EASY.
IT'S LIKE THROWAWAY CLOTHES.

152
00:05:49,082 --> 00:05:52,285
Toccara: MY CLOTHES
ARE FABULOUS, REBECCA.

153
00:05:52,285 --> 00:05:53,620
Rebecca:
YOU'RE B.S.-ING ME.

154
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,055
TOCCARA LACKS A LITTLE BIT
OF PERSONAL STYLE.

155
00:05:56,055 --> 00:05:58,091
I DON'T SEE ANYTHING REALLY
DRESSY TO PULL ANYTHING

156
00:05:58,091 --> 00:06:00,660
OUT OF YOUR CLOSET
THAT'S LIKE, "WOW."

157
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,996
WHEN I LOOK AT YOU, YOU'RE JUST
LIKE ECLECTIC COMFORTABLE.

158
00:06:02,996 --> 00:06:04,097
Eva: MM-HMM.

159
00:06:04,097 --> 00:06:05,899
Rebecca: EVA NEEDS
TO BROADEN HER HORIZONS.

160
00:06:05,899 --> 00:06:08,201
THESE ARE OKAY, BUT THEY
DON'T SAY MUCH.

161
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:12,739
I'D LIKE TO SEE EVA OWN UP
TO HER POTENTIAL STARDOM.

162
00:06:12,739 --> 00:06:14,674
I WANNA SEE EVA IN SOMETHING
THAT NOBODY ELSE HAS.

163
00:06:14,674 --> 00:06:15,975
Eva: OKAY.

164
00:06:15,975 --> 00:06:18,611
Amanda: I'M PROBABLY ONE
OF THE MOST UNIQUE GIRLS HERE.

165
00:06:18,611 --> 00:06:19,812
I'M LEGALLY BLIND.

166
00:06:19,812 --> 00:06:22,949
Paul: YOU HAVE A UNIQUE
OPPORTUNITY FOR PEOPLE

167
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:24,751
WHO ARE IN
SIMILAR SITUATIONS

168
00:06:24,751 --> 00:06:28,121
TO BECOME, YOU KNOW,
AN EMBLEM FOR SUCCESS.

169
00:06:28,121 --> 00:06:29,923
Rebecca:
THIS IS LIKE SO HIGH SCHOOL.

170
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:31,224
GIRL, YOU GOTTA GROW UP.

171
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:33,593
NORELLE'S STYLE--
IT'S SO YOUTHFUL,

172
00:06:33,593 --> 00:06:35,295
THAT IT'S CHILDLIKE.

173
00:06:35,295 --> 00:06:36,629
I DON'T SEE ANYTHING HERE
THAT SAYS,

174
00:06:36,629 --> 00:06:38,765
"I CAN BE
A SOPHISTICATED WOMAN."

175
00:06:38,765 --> 00:06:39,866
Nicole: I LIKE ART.

176
00:06:39,866 --> 00:06:41,734
I LIKE STUFF
THAT'S NOT REALLY NORMAL.

177
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:43,036
IT'S NOT REALLY
POP CULTURE.

178
00:06:43,036 --> 00:06:44,737
I DON'T KNOW IF
THAT'S GONNA BE A PROBLEM

179
00:06:44,737 --> 00:06:46,139
WHERE I HAVE TO, LIKE,
ACT LIKE

180
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:49,008
I LIKE JESSICA SIMPSON
OR SOMETHING. EVEN LIKE--

181
00:06:49,008 --> 00:06:51,644
Hampton: IF YOU ARE ASKED
A QUESTION ABOUT POP CULTURE,

182
00:06:51,644 --> 00:06:52,812
YOU CAN ANSWER
THAT QUESTION

183
00:06:52,812 --> 00:06:55,882
THAT'S TRUE TO YOURSELF,
BUT AT THE SAME TIME,

184
00:06:55,882 --> 00:06:58,351
YOU'RE NOT BEING SORT OF A JERK
IN FRONT OF A REPORTER.

185
00:06:58,351 --> 00:06:59,586
Paul: NO NEGATIVES.

186
00:07:01,554 --> 00:07:03,389
Rebecca: YOU'RE KIND OF
A LITTLE BIT COUNTRY

187
00:07:03,389 --> 00:07:04,390
AND A LITTLE BIT
ROCK 'N' ROLL.

188
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:06,593
Ann:
OH, I HAVE EVERYTHING.

189
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:08,261
Rebecca: I THINK YOU NEED
TO MIX UP YOUR WARDROBE

190
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,930
A LITTLE BIT MORE THAN JUST
WHAT'S COMFORTABLE AND CASUAL.

191
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,198
I DON'T SEE,
LIKE, ONE DRESS

192
00:07:12,198 --> 00:07:13,600
THAT YOU COULD WEAR
ON A CASTING.

193
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,867
Toccara: I AM
A FULL-FIGURED MODEL

194
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:16,669
AND JUST WANTED SOME
FEEDBACK ON THAT.

195
00:07:16,669 --> 00:07:18,638
Paul: A LOT OF THE MORE
CLASSICAL HOUSES

196
00:07:18,638 --> 00:07:20,039
ARE CUTTING PLUS SIZES.

197
00:07:20,039 --> 00:07:22,475
YOU SHOULD HAVE A WONDERFUL
CAREER FOR YOURSELF, ABSOLUTELY.

198
00:07:22,475 --> 00:07:23,776
Toccara: THANK YOU.

199
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:26,346
AND SHE WAS LIKE,
"YOU DON'T HAVE ANY DRESSES.

200
00:07:26,346 --> 00:07:28,815
YOU DON'T HAVE ANY SKIRTS."

201
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:30,516
Yaya: LIKE, I KNOW
THERE HAS TO BE VERSATILITY.

202
00:07:30,516 --> 00:07:31,818
- I KNOW THAT.
- Toccara: MM-HMM.

203
00:07:31,818 --> 00:07:33,753
Yaya: BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN
I'M GONNA WALK AROUND

204
00:07:33,753 --> 00:07:34,954
LOOKING LIKE
SOMETHING THAT I'M NOT

205
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:35,955
OR THAT I'M NOT TRYING
TO REPRESENT.

206
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,390
Rebecca:
THEY'LL SEE THE BIG HAIR

207
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,992
AND THEY SEE THE AFRICAN PRINT
AND IT'S LIKE, "OH, MY GOD."

208
00:07:38,992 --> 00:07:40,927
Yaya: I FELT LIKE
SHE WAS TALKING ABOUT
THAT I WOULDN'T FIT IN.

209
00:07:40,927 --> 00:07:42,228
I WAS LIKE, "YEAH,
THAT'S THE WHOLE POINT.

210
00:07:42,228 --> 00:07:45,298
- I'M NOT TRYING TO FIT IN."
- Rebecca: OKAY, GALS.

211
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:48,001
I HAD SUCH A NICE TIME
GETTING TO KNOW YOU.

212
00:07:48,001 --> 00:07:50,136
- Paul: MAKE MILLIONS, OKAY?
- Women: THANK YOU!

213
00:07:51,938 --> 00:07:53,206
Yaya: I DON'T CARE.

214
00:07:59,278 --> 00:08:01,881
Ann: TONIGHT WE'RE HEADING
TO UNCLE JACK'S STEAKHOUSE

215
00:08:01,881 --> 00:08:05,218
FOR DINNER
WITH THE SEVEN OF US.

216
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:06,519
OKAY, IT'S, LIKE,
SETTING IN

217
00:08:06,519 --> 00:08:08,421
THAT THERE'S REALLY
ONLY SEVEN OF US.

218
00:08:08,421 --> 00:08:11,090
LIKE, I'M LOOKING AROUND LIKE,
"WHERE IS EVERYONE ELSE?"

219
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:12,859
AFTER LAST WEEK,

220
00:08:12,859 --> 00:08:15,395
MY WHOLE, LIKE, OUTLOOK
ON THIS HAS CHANGED.

221
00:08:15,395 --> 00:08:16,729
- Tyra: THAT'S NICE.
- Nigel: BEAUTIFUL.

222
00:08:16,729 --> 00:08:17,930
Janice: BEST ONE YET.

223
00:08:17,930 --> 00:08:19,999
Ann: AS LONG AS
I KEEP IMPROVING,

224
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:22,235
I THINK I HAVE A REALLY GOOD
CHANCE TO WIN THIS.

225
00:08:22,235 --> 00:08:23,569
TO THE SEVEN.

226
00:08:23,569 --> 00:08:24,570
Women: TO THE SEVEN.

227
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:25,672
Norelle: CLINK.

228
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:32,278
Women: (scream)

229
00:08:32,278 --> 00:08:33,946
- Tyra: HI, EVERYBODY.
- Women: HEY! HI!

230
00:08:33,946 --> 00:08:35,081
Tyra: GIVE ME HUGS,
EVERYBODY.

231
00:08:35,081 --> 00:08:36,549
Eva: HEY, HOW YOU DOING?

232
00:08:36,549 --> 00:08:39,719
Nicole: MISS TYRA POPS IN AND
SURPRISES EVERYBODY AT DINNER.

233
00:08:39,719 --> 00:08:41,054
Tyra: SO WHAT'S GOING ON?

234
00:08:41,054 --> 00:08:42,655
ACTUALLY, I WANNA
TASTE YOU GUYS' FOOD.

235
00:08:42,655 --> 00:08:44,290
- IS THAT ALL RIGHT WITH YOU?
- Yaya: THIS SALAD--

236
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:46,025
Tyra: I'M NOTORIOUS
FOR THIS, YOU GUYS.

237
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,294
I, LIKE, EAT OFF
EVERYBODY'S PLATES.

238
00:08:48,294 --> 00:08:50,763
Norelle: OKAY, WHAT DID WE
REALLY GET OURSELVES INTO?

239
00:08:50,763 --> 00:08:53,099
LIKE, HOW MUCH IS THIS--
NOT LIKE,

240
00:08:53,099 --> 00:08:54,701
IS THIS GONNA CHANGE
OUR LIVES AND AFFECT US,

241
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,536
LIKE, I'VE LEARNED
SO MUCH, AND I, LIKE,

242
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,804
FEEL SO BLESSED TO BE HERE
'CAUSE THERE'S

243
00:08:57,804 --> 00:08:59,372
SO MANY THINGS ABOUT,
LIKE, THIS INDUSTRY

244
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:00,707
THAT I HAD NO IDEA.

245
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:04,077
Tyra: SEE, WHAT YOU GUYS
ARE SEEING ARE THE CRITICISM

246
00:09:04,077 --> 00:09:06,512
THAT A MODEL GETS WHEN SHE
WALKS OUT THE DOOR.

247
00:09:06,512 --> 00:09:07,847
THE ONLY THING IS
YOU GUYS ARE RIGHT THERE

248
00:09:07,847 --> 00:09:09,549
- AND YOU HEAR IT.
- Eva: RIGHT.

249
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,417
Tyra: BUT AS DIFFICULT
AS IT IS, AND AS HARD AS IT IS

250
00:09:11,417 --> 00:09:13,119
TO HEAR THAT CRITICISM
THAT'S SO HARSH--

251
00:09:13,119 --> 00:09:15,655
Toccara: YOU LOOK LIKE A BOY.
YOU LOOK LIKE A LINEBACKER.

252
00:09:15,655 --> 00:09:17,323
Tyra: BUT, UM,
IT'S A LUXURY,

253
00:09:17,323 --> 00:09:18,658
AND YOU GUYS NEED
TO LOOK AT IT AS,

254
00:09:18,658 --> 00:09:20,727
"WOW, I'M HEARING WHAT
PEOPLE SAY ABOUT ME."

255
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,395
IT REALLY DOES
CHANGE YOUR LIFE.

256
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:23,529
Toccara: SOMEONE SAID, UM,

257
00:09:23,529 --> 00:09:25,498
AMERICA'S NOT READY FOR
A PLUS-SIZED TOP MODEL.

258
00:09:25,498 --> 00:09:26,999
CAN YOU GIVE ME
A COMMENT?

259
00:09:26,999 --> 00:09:28,234
Tyra: TO ME,
THE WHOLE PLUS-SIZED MARKET

260
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,136
KINDA REMINDS ME OF, LIKE,

261
00:09:30,136 --> 00:09:32,472
BEING A BLACK MODEL
FORTY YEARS AGO.

262
00:09:32,472 --> 00:09:33,806
YOU KNOW,
WHEN PEOPLE WERE LIKE,

263
00:09:33,806 --> 00:09:35,908
"AMERICA'S JUST NOT READY
FOR A BLACK SUPERMODEL."

264
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:36,909
AND THEY PROBABLY
WERE SAYING THAT

265
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:38,845
BEFORE BEVERLY JOHNSON,
AND BEFORE IMAN.

266
00:09:38,845 --> 00:09:39,912
THOSE ARE LIKE PIONEERS.

267
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:42,048
NAOMI SIMS
IS ANOTHER WOMAN.

268
00:09:42,048 --> 00:09:44,083
SO YOU HAVE A LOT
WORKING AGAINST YOU.

269
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,585
I HAVE A LOT WORKING
AGAINST ME, TOO,

270
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:46,786
EVEN BEING A BLACK MODEL,

271
00:09:46,786 --> 00:09:48,888
- EVEN IN THE NEW MILLENNIUM.
- Eva: RIGHT.

272
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:50,656
Tyra: SO I HAVE TO
WORK HARDER, STRIVE HARDER.

273
00:09:50,656 --> 00:09:53,126
AND AS A PLUS-SIZED MODEL THAT'S
TRYING TO MAKE IT TO THE TOP,

274
00:09:53,126 --> 00:09:55,294
YOU CAN'T BE AS GOOD
AS THE GIRLS AT THIS TABLE.

275
00:09:55,294 --> 00:09:56,696
YOU HAVE TO BE BETTER THAN

276
00:09:56,696 --> 00:09:58,731
TO GET THE SAME AMOUNT
OF RESPECT THAT THEY GET.

277
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:00,533
Toccara: I LISTEN
TO CONSTRUCTIVE CRITICISM,

278
00:10:00,533 --> 00:10:02,201
BUT I NEVER LET IT
BREAK MY SPIRIT.

279
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:04,804
BUT I'M WORKING
AGAINST A LOT OF ODDS,

280
00:10:04,804 --> 00:10:06,339
AND SO I HAVE TO BE
REALLY FOCUSED

281
00:10:06,339 --> 00:10:07,707
AND I HAVE TO BE
ON TOP OF MY STUFF.

282
00:10:07,707 --> 00:10:11,477
I HAVE TO BE A HUNDRED FEET
AHEAD OF THE REST.

283
00:10:16,125 --> 00:10:18,094
Ann: TYRA MAIL!

284
00:10:18,094 --> 00:10:19,128
Eva:
WHY IS EVERYBODY HERE?

285
00:10:19,128 --> 00:10:20,663
Ann: NICOLE WANTS
TO READ IT.

286
00:10:20,663 --> 00:10:22,732
- MAKE ONE UP. MAKE ONE UP.
- Nicole: OKAY.

287
00:10:22,732 --> 00:10:23,733
Ann: (whispering)
SAY, "PACK YOUR BAGS.

288
00:10:23,733 --> 00:10:24,734
YOU HAVE 20 MINUTES."

289
00:10:24,734 --> 00:10:26,536
Eva: ANN, I AND NICOLE

290
00:10:26,536 --> 00:10:29,372
PLAY A PRACTICAL JOKE ON
THE HOUSE WITH THE TYRA MAIL.

291
00:10:29,372 --> 00:10:30,473
Nicole: "PACK YOUR BAGS.

292
00:10:30,473 --> 00:10:33,009
YOU HAVE 20 MINUTES
TO BE IN EUROPE!"

293
00:10:33,009 --> 00:10:35,812
Eva: OH, MY GOD!
OH, MY GOD!

294
00:10:35,812 --> 00:10:37,747
Nicole:
WE HAVE 20 MINUTES!

295
00:10:37,747 --> 00:10:39,082
Toccara: 20 MINUTES?

296
00:10:39,082 --> 00:10:41,150
OH, MY! ARE YOU LYING?

297
00:10:41,150 --> 00:10:43,319
Women: (shouting)

298
00:10:43,319 --> 00:10:44,520
Nicole: NO, I--

299
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,456
Toccara: YOU LYING?
YOU'RE A...

300
00:10:47,523 --> 00:10:48,524
Ann: WE'RE GOING TO EUROPE.

301
00:10:48,524 --> 00:10:50,059
Toccara:
Y'ALL ARE-- THEY LYING.

302
00:10:50,059 --> 00:10:53,029
- YEAH, THEY'RE LYING.
- Ann: (laughs)

303
00:10:53,029 --> 00:10:55,598
Amanda: LIKE, "HA HA HA.
REAL FUNNY."

304
00:10:55,598 --> 00:10:57,367
Eva: (laughs)

305
00:10:57,367 --> 00:10:59,235
THE WHOLE HOUSE
WAS SO PISSED.

306
00:10:59,235 --> 00:11:01,971
(laughs)

307
00:11:01,971 --> 00:11:03,473
Yaya: LIKE, SERIOUSLY,

308
00:11:03,473 --> 00:11:05,975
COMING TO THIS COMPETITION
I DID NOT REALIZE

309
00:11:05,975 --> 00:11:08,177
THAT I WAS GONNA FEEL LIKE
I WAS IN JUNIOR HIGH SCHOOL.

310
00:11:08,177 --> 00:11:10,713
Ann: I'M GONNA THROW UP
FROM LAUGHING SO HARD.

311
00:11:10,713 --> 00:11:12,548
Eva: NO ONE WANTS
TO HAVE FUN AROUND HERE.

312
00:11:14,384 --> 00:11:15,818
OUR TYRA MAIL READS,

313
00:11:15,818 --> 00:11:20,023
"GET READY FOR A 21st CENTURY
RED CARPET RIDE."

314
00:11:27,196 --> 00:11:28,631
Ann: WE ENDED UP
GOING TO CENTURY 21,

315
00:11:28,631 --> 00:11:31,934
- A DEPARTMENT STORE.
- Women: HEY.

316
00:11:31,934 --> 00:11:35,104
Nicole: SO WE ARRIVE,
AND REBECCA WEINBERG
IS WAITING FOR US.

317
00:11:35,104 --> 00:11:37,874
Rebecca: ALL RIGHT, LADIES,
WELCOME TO CENTURY 21.

318
00:11:37,874 --> 00:11:39,942
THIS IS LIKE
THE BEST SHOPPING PLACE EVER.

319
00:11:39,942 --> 00:11:42,078
Amanda: CENTURY 21
IS WHERE YOU CAN FIND

320
00:11:42,078 --> 00:11:44,881
BIG DESIGNERS FOR
RIDICULOUSLY CHEAP.

321
00:11:44,881 --> 00:11:46,749
Rebecca: HERE'S
THE CHALLENGE, RIGHT?

322
00:11:46,749 --> 00:11:48,584
YOU GOTTA PUT TOGETHER
A HEAD-TO-TOE LOOK

323
00:11:48,584 --> 00:11:49,986
FOR A DAYTIME EVENT.

324
00:11:49,986 --> 00:11:53,122
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE 15 MINUTES
TO PULL YOUR LOOKS TOGETHER.

325
00:11:53,122 --> 00:11:54,657
THIS STORE
HAS GOT AMAZING STUFF.

326
00:11:54,657 --> 00:11:55,992
Toccara: LIKE, "OH, MY GOD.
THIS IS SO GREAT."

327
00:11:55,992 --> 00:11:58,127
THEY'VE GOT ALL THESE CLOTHES
AND ALL THESE DESIGNERS.

328
00:11:58,127 --> 00:12:00,229
I'M LIKE, "WOW, I'M ABOUT
TO HAVE A FIELD DAY."

329
00:12:00,229 --> 00:12:01,297
Rebecca: GO!

330
00:12:09,772 --> 00:12:13,443
Ann: REBECCA SAYS THAT I NEED
TO, LIKE, HAVE DRESSY CLOTHES,

331
00:12:13,443 --> 00:12:15,044
SO I'M JUST GONNA FOCUS
ON THAT.

332
00:12:15,044 --> 00:12:17,413
Norelle: OH,
I LOOK LIKE A FREAK.

333
00:12:17,413 --> 00:12:19,449
Yaya: I TOOK MY CONVERSATION
WITH REBECCA

334
00:12:19,449 --> 00:12:21,517
AS JUST THAT--
A CONVERSATION.

335
00:12:21,517 --> 00:12:24,620
NOT HOW I HAD TO PRESENT MYSELF
IN ORDER TO BE SUCCESSFUL.

336
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:29,192
I'VE BEEN SUCCESSFUL
WITHOUT COMPROMISING WHO I AM.

337
00:12:31,861 --> 00:12:35,298
Toccara: IT TOOK ME FOREVER
TO FIND MY SIZE.

338
00:12:37,934 --> 00:12:39,936
I DIDN'T WANT TO
BLOW OFF THE COMPETITION,

339
00:12:39,936 --> 00:12:41,604
BUT IT WAS REALLY
A DOWNER.

340
00:12:41,604 --> 00:12:43,739
Rebecca: I WAS A LITTLE
WORRIED ABOUT TOCCARA

341
00:12:43,739 --> 00:12:45,942
BECAUSE HER PACE
WAS VERY SLOW,

342
00:12:45,942 --> 00:12:47,443
WHEREAS
THE OTHER GIRLS WERE

343
00:12:47,443 --> 00:12:50,446
FROM ONE END OF THE ROOM
TO THE OTHER.

344
00:12:50,446 --> 00:12:51,447
THREE...

345
00:12:51,447 --> 00:12:52,448
TWO...

346
00:12:52,448 --> 00:12:54,117
TIME'S UP RIGHT NOW!

347
00:12:54,117 --> 00:12:56,319
WHAT YOU HAVE
IS WHAT YOU'LL WEAR.

348
00:12:56,319 --> 00:12:57,954
YOU'VE GOT A LIMO
COMING FOR YOU.

349
00:12:57,954 --> 00:12:59,322
Women: (gasp)

350
00:12:59,322 --> 00:13:01,624
Rebecca: LET'S GO, COME ON.
YOU HAVE VERY LITTLE TIME.

351
00:13:01,624 --> 00:13:04,627
Nicole: WE HAVE TO GO HOME,
GET READY FOR OUR DAYTIME EVENT.

352
00:13:05,761 --> 00:13:07,530
Toccara: I WAS, LIKE,
FRUSTRATED.

353
00:13:07,530 --> 00:13:09,165
THE DRESSES--EITHER
THEY WERE BODY-FITTING

354
00:13:09,165 --> 00:13:10,633
OR THEY WERE LIKE BIG CLOTH.

355
00:13:10,633 --> 00:13:11,901
Eva: MM-HMM.
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

356
00:13:11,901 --> 00:13:13,836
I DO FEEL SORRY FOR TOCCARA,

357
00:13:13,836 --> 00:13:16,806
BUT BY THE SAME TOKEN,
YOU GOTTA STEP IT UP.

358
00:13:16,806 --> 00:13:17,907
IT WAS FASHIONABLE.

359
00:13:17,907 --> 00:13:19,408
IT'S FASHION.
IT LOOKS GOOD.

360
00:13:19,408 --> 00:13:20,843
Toccara:
EVA IS VERY SWEET.

361
00:13:20,843 --> 00:13:25,181
SHE'S TURNED OUT TO REALLY BE
OPTIMISTIC ABOUT ME.

362
00:13:25,181 --> 00:13:26,949
Eva:
TOCCARA, TOCCARA.

363
00:13:26,949 --> 00:13:28,017
Toccara: (laughs)

364
00:13:28,017 --> 00:13:29,385
AND THAT WAS VERY HELPFUL.

365
00:13:31,888 --> 00:13:34,090
Yaya: WE'RE NOT SURE
WHERE WE'RE GOING YET.

366
00:13:36,626 --> 00:13:39,529
Eva: WE PULL UP IN A LIMO,
WALK IN.

367
00:13:39,529 --> 00:13:42,064
Men: EVA! EVA! EVA!

368
00:13:42,064 --> 00:13:44,467
Eva:
IT'S A RED CARPET EVENT.

369
00:13:44,467 --> 00:13:46,569
ALL YOU HEAR IS,
"EVA! EVA! EVA!"

370
00:13:46,569 --> 00:13:48,771
EVERYBODY'S SCREAMING YOUR NAME
AND TAKING PICTURES

371
00:13:48,771 --> 00:13:50,573
AND WANTING YOU
TO LOOK HERE AND LOOK THERE,

372
00:13:50,573 --> 00:13:53,376
AND A BIG SCREEN
WITH MY FACE UP THERE.

373
00:13:53,376 --> 00:13:54,810
Sarah:
HI, EVA, "US WEEKLY."

374
00:13:54,810 --> 00:13:56,846
- DO YOU HAVE A FEW MOMENTS?
- Eva: SURE.

375
00:13:56,846 --> 00:13:57,980
Sarah: SO WHO ARE
YOU WEARING TODAY?

376
00:13:57,980 --> 00:13:59,615
- YOU LOOK FANTASTIC.
- Eva: VALENTINO.

377
00:13:59,615 --> 00:14:02,018
Sarah: WHO'S THE MOST
ANNOYING GIRL IN THE GROUP?

378
00:14:02,018 --> 00:14:04,387
Eva: WHAT KIND OF FREAKIN'
QUESTIONS ARE THOSE?

379
00:14:04,387 --> 00:14:06,122
PAUL AND HAMPTON
HAVE ALREADY PREPPED ME

380
00:14:06,122 --> 00:14:08,124
ON HOW TO ANSWER
THOSE QUESTIONS.

381
00:14:08,124 --> 00:14:09,692
Eva: EVERYONE'S
EQUALLY ANNOYING.

382
00:14:09,692 --> 00:14:10,893
NEVER DISCLOSE A NAME.

383
00:14:10,893 --> 00:14:13,262
YOU NEVER DO ANYTHING
TO PINPOINT ANYONE.

384
00:14:13,262 --> 00:14:14,730
Sarah: THAT'S FANTASTIC.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

385
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:15,798
Eva: THANK YOU.

386
00:14:15,798 --> 00:14:17,700
Men:
EVA! EVA, OVER HERE!

387
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,202
YAYA! YAYA!

388
00:14:19,202 --> 00:14:22,171
Yaya: I WAS NOT PREPARED
FOR WHAT WE WALKED INTO.

389
00:14:22,171 --> 00:14:24,440
AND THERE WERE JUST
FLASHES, FLASHES, FLASHES,

390
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,576
AND I WAS LIKE,
"HA HA HA. WOW."

391
00:14:26,576 --> 00:14:27,710
Sarah:
WHO ARE YOU WEARING?

392
00:14:27,710 --> 00:14:29,512
Yaya: I'M WEARING
MOSTLY MOSCHINO TODAY.

393
00:14:29,512 --> 00:14:30,746
Sarah: WHO'S THE PERSON
YOU HAVE THE BIGGEST PROBLEM

394
00:14:30,746 --> 00:14:31,914
WITH IN THE HOUSE?

395
00:14:31,914 --> 00:14:33,716
Yaya: I DON'T HAVE
A PROBLEM WITH ANYONE.

396
00:14:33,716 --> 00:14:34,850
Sarah: GREAT,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

397
00:14:34,850 --> 00:14:36,018
Yaya: THANK YOU,
MY PLEASURE.

398
00:14:36,018 --> 00:14:38,988
Man:
HERE. YAYA! YAYA!

399
00:14:38,988 --> 00:14:41,757
NORELLE, LOOK HERE!
NORELLE!

400
00:14:41,757 --> 00:14:42,992
- Sarah: SO YOU LOOK GREAT.
- Norelle: OH, THANK YOU.

401
00:14:42,992 --> 00:14:43,993
Sarah: WHO ARE YOU WEARING?

402
00:14:43,993 --> 00:14:45,461
Norelle: THIS IS
A MOSCHINO JACKET.

403
00:14:45,461 --> 00:14:46,929
Sarah: NOW WHO WOULD SAY
ARE THE PEOPLE

404
00:14:46,929 --> 00:14:50,032
YOU DON'T CLICK WITH
QUITE AS MUCH?

405
00:14:50,032 --> 00:14:52,134
Norelle: UM...

406
00:14:52,134 --> 00:14:54,604
HER NAME IS YAYA.

407
00:14:54,604 --> 00:14:56,672
NOT THAT WE DON'T CLICK.
SHE'S JUST KIND OF STANDOFFISH.

408
00:14:56,672 --> 00:14:59,375
Sarah: NORELLE GAVE A NAME
THAT COULD MAKE HER LOOK BAD.

409
00:14:59,375 --> 00:15:00,610
- THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
- Norelle: OH, THANK YOU.

410
00:15:00,610 --> 00:15:02,678
Men:
NORELLE! NORELLE!

411
00:15:02,678 --> 00:15:04,747
AMANDA! AMANDA!

412
00:15:04,747 --> 00:15:06,682
LOOK OVER HERE, AMANDA!

413
00:15:06,682 --> 00:15:08,384
Sarah: ARE THERE MOMENTS
WHEN YOU WANT TO GIVE UP

414
00:15:08,384 --> 00:15:09,952
OR SCREAM AT SOMEONE?

415
00:15:09,952 --> 00:15:12,154
- Amanda: FOR SURE.
- Sarah: ANYONE IN PARTICULAR?

416
00:15:12,154 --> 00:15:13,256
Amanda: THAT'S CONFIDENTIAL.

417
00:15:13,256 --> 00:15:14,557
Sarah: GREAT,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

418
00:15:14,557 --> 00:15:16,225
- Amanda: THANK YOU.
- Men: AMANDA, OVER HERE!

419
00:15:16,225 --> 00:15:18,094
OVER HERE, AMANDA.

420
00:15:19,762 --> 00:15:22,665
ANN! ANN! OVER HERE!

421
00:15:22,665 --> 00:15:23,799
Sarah:
WHO ARE YOU WEARING?

422
00:15:23,799 --> 00:15:26,168
Ann: THE JACKET'S...
PURSE--VALENTINA.

423
00:15:26,168 --> 00:15:27,737
Sarah: AND HAVE YOU SEEN
YOURSELF ON THE BIG SCREEN?

424
00:15:27,737 --> 00:15:29,038
Ann: NO, I HAVE NOT.

425
00:15:31,007 --> 00:15:32,808
THAT'S A FIRST.

426
00:15:32,808 --> 00:15:34,710
Sarah: HAVE YOU HAD
ANY FIGHTS WITH ANYONE?

427
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:36,212
Ann: THERE HASN'T
REALLY BEEN ANYONE

428
00:15:36,212 --> 00:15:37,980
THAT I'VE, YOU KNOW,
BUTTED HEADS WITH.

429
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:39,115
Men:
NICOLE! NICOLE!

430
00:15:39,115 --> 00:15:41,384
OVER HERE! NICOLE!

431
00:15:41,384 --> 00:15:43,119
Sarah: WHO'S CAUSING
THE MOST TENSION IN THE HOUSE?

432
00:15:43,119 --> 00:15:45,288
Nicole: YOU CAN'T REALLY
PIN IT ON ONE SPECIFIC PERSON.

433
00:15:45,288 --> 00:15:46,756
- Sarah: THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
- Nicole: THANK YOU.

434
00:15:46,756 --> 00:15:48,190
Men: NICOLE! NICOLE!

435
00:15:49,659 --> 00:15:52,194
TOCCARA! TOCCARA!

436
00:15:52,194 --> 00:15:54,830
Toccara: I'M WEARING
JOHN PAUL GAWTI-ERRE.

437
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:56,699
GAWTIE--
(laughs)

438
00:15:56,699 --> 00:15:57,933
Sarah: SO TOCCARA--

439
00:15:57,933 --> 00:15:59,368
SHE DIDN'T KNOW
HOW TO PRONOUNCE

440
00:15:59,368 --> 00:16:01,837
JEAN-PAUL GAULTIER,
AND THAT'S REALLY IMPORTANT.

441
00:16:01,837 --> 00:16:03,072
IT MAKES YOU LOOK
VERY SILLY.

442
00:16:03,072 --> 00:16:04,507
- THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
- Toccara: THANK YOU.

443
00:16:04,507 --> 00:16:05,608
Men: HERE! HERE!

444
00:16:05,608 --> 00:16:06,976
Amanda: YEAH.

445
00:16:06,976 --> 00:16:08,611
Eva: SHE WAS SAYING
LIKE, "WHO'S ANNOYING?"

446
00:16:08,611 --> 00:16:10,079
AND I'M LIKE, "WHAT DO YOU
MEAN WHO'S ANNOYING?"

447
00:16:10,079 --> 00:16:11,647
Yaya: SHE WAS FUNNY, THOUGH.
SHE WAS TRYING TO--

448
00:16:11,647 --> 00:16:14,517
Eva: SHE WAS TRYING
TO READ YOU, BOY.

449
00:16:14,517 --> 00:16:16,252
Norelle: I SAID
YOUR NAME IN MINE. HA!

450
00:16:16,252 --> 00:16:17,653
Yaya: WHAT DID YOU SAY?

451
00:16:17,653 --> 00:16:19,689
Norelle: I SAID,
"YAYA HAS A WALL BUILT UP

452
00:16:19,689 --> 00:16:20,690
WHICH IS UNDERSTANDABLE."

453
00:16:20,690 --> 00:16:22,258
Yaya: OH, A COMMENT. HA.

454
00:16:22,258 --> 00:16:24,093
NORELLE GAVE A NAME,
WHICH WAS MINE,

455
00:16:24,093 --> 00:16:25,761
AND I WASN'T
REALLY SURPRISED

456
00:16:25,761 --> 00:16:29,198
BECAUSE I SEE HER
AS BEING VERY FLAKY.

457
00:16:29,198 --> 00:16:31,467
I JUST NEVER MADE
A CONNECTION WITH HER.

458
00:16:31,467 --> 00:16:33,402
Sarah: HELLO, EVERYONE.

459
00:16:33,402 --> 00:16:34,537
WELL, IT'S BEEN REALLY
GREAT MEETING YOU

460
00:16:34,537 --> 00:16:35,905
AND SEEING YOU AT WORK.

461
00:16:35,905 --> 00:16:38,407
I'VE SEEN MANY RED CARPETS,
AND IT'S A SCARY PLACE.

462
00:16:38,407 --> 00:16:40,242
WELL, EVA,
YOU DID VERY WELL.

463
00:16:40,242 --> 00:16:41,444
YOU LOOKED GREAT.

464
00:16:41,444 --> 00:16:43,746
YOU WALKED DOWN THE RUNWAY
REALLY NICELY.

465
00:16:43,746 --> 00:16:46,349
NORELLE, YOU WERE
THE ONLY ONE TO NAME NAMES.

466
00:16:46,349 --> 00:16:48,918
YOU DON'T WANT TO BE SEEN
AS BITCHY.

467
00:16:48,918 --> 00:16:51,687
AMANDA, YOU OBVIOUSLY LOVED
BEING ON THE RED CARPET.

468
00:16:51,687 --> 00:16:52,988
YOU POSED VERY WELL.

469
00:16:52,988 --> 00:16:54,924
YAYA, YOU, AGAIN,
ANOTHER PERSON

470
00:16:54,924 --> 00:16:56,926
WHO REALLY ENJOYED
THE RED CARPET.

471
00:16:56,926 --> 00:16:59,395
I DETECTED A DEFINITE
DIVA ATTITUDE THERE

472
00:16:59,395 --> 00:17:01,530
WHICH SOMETIMES
COMES ACROSS BADLY.

473
00:17:01,530 --> 00:17:03,933
Eva: YAYA--
SHE HAD DIVA SYNDROME

474
00:17:03,933 --> 00:17:05,601
WHICH TRANSLATED
AS A BITCH.

475
00:17:05,601 --> 00:17:07,670
Sarah: TOCCARA,
IF YOU'RE A MODEL,

476
00:17:07,670 --> 00:17:08,938
AND YOU CAN'T PRONOUNCE
THE NAME

477
00:17:08,938 --> 00:17:10,873
OF THE PERSON WHO'S
DESIGNED YOUR CLOTHES,

478
00:17:10,873 --> 00:17:12,208
IT'S NOT GOOD.

479
00:17:12,208 --> 00:17:14,242
NICOLE,
YOU'VE GOT A LOVELY SMILE.

480
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:17,179
YOU DIDN'T QUITE GIVE ACROSS
YOUR WHOLE PERSONALITY.

481
00:17:17,179 --> 00:17:18,748
ANN, YOU LOOKED GREAT.

482
00:17:18,748 --> 00:17:21,384
YOU MOVE VERY WELL,
POSED VERY WELL.

483
00:17:21,384 --> 00:17:23,085
SO ON TO THE GOOD STUFF,

484
00:17:23,085 --> 00:17:25,588
THE PERSON WHO
DID THE BEST TODAY...

485
00:17:25,588 --> 00:17:26,955
IS YAYA.

486
00:17:26,955 --> 00:17:28,124
Yaya: OOH!

487
00:17:28,124 --> 00:17:29,592
Eva: SHE WINS?

488
00:17:29,592 --> 00:17:30,793
YOU SEE THIS FACE?

489
00:17:30,793 --> 00:17:33,329
THIS IS A CONFUSED FACE.

490
00:17:33,329 --> 00:17:34,930
Ann: SO SHE'S WON
THREE IN A ROW.

491
00:17:34,930 --> 00:17:36,465
ARE YOU KIDDING?

492
00:17:36,465 --> 00:17:37,767
Yaya:
IT FEELS GOOD TO WIN.

493
00:17:37,767 --> 00:17:39,602
I WANNA BE AMERICA'S
NEXT TOP MODEL.

494
00:17:39,602 --> 00:17:40,770
Sarah: YOU'VE GOT
A SURPRISE WAITING FOR YOU

495
00:17:40,770 --> 00:17:42,037
BACK AT THE HOUSE.

496
00:17:42,037 --> 00:17:44,540
AND YOU JUST NEED NOW
TO CHOOSE ONE OTHER PERSON

497
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:46,041
TO ENJOY THAT SURPRISE
WITH YOU.

498
00:17:48,611 --> 00:17:49,945
Yaya: NORELLE.

499
00:17:49,945 --> 00:17:51,647
BECAUSE SHE THINKS--
I DON'T KNOW WHY SHE THINKS--

500
00:17:51,647 --> 00:17:53,849
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

501
00:17:53,849 --> 00:17:55,785
I PICKED HER JUST
TO MAKE HER FEEL, YOU KNOW,

502
00:17:55,785 --> 00:17:57,887
LIKE I'M MORE APPROACHABLE
OR WARMER.

503
00:17:57,887 --> 00:17:59,588
Sarah:
SO THANKS VERY MUCH. BYE.

504
00:17:59,588 --> 00:18:00,589
Women: IT WAS NICE
TO MEET YOU.

505
00:18:01,991 --> 00:18:03,058
(knock on door)

506
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:06,228
- Man: HI.
- Eva: HI.

507
00:18:06,228 --> 00:18:07,463
Man: I'M BRIAN.
THIS IS MARK.

508
00:18:07,463 --> 00:18:08,464
- Eva: HI.
- Mark: HI THERE.

509
00:18:08,464 --> 00:18:10,132
Eva: EVA. YAYA!

510
00:18:10,132 --> 00:18:11,434
- Nicole: HI.
- Brian: HI, EVERYBODY.

511
00:18:11,434 --> 00:18:14,737
- DO WE HAVE A WINNER IN HERE?
- Yaya: I AM.

512
00:18:14,737 --> 00:18:16,972
Brian:
YOUR PRIZE TONIGHT

513
00:18:16,972 --> 00:18:18,841
IS SOME PERSONAL CHEFING

514
00:18:18,841 --> 00:18:20,943
- RIGHT FROM NU KITCHEN.
- Yaya: OOH!

515
00:18:20,943 --> 00:18:24,246
Norelle: YAYA'S PRIZE
IS DINNER FROM NU KITCHEN.

516
00:18:24,246 --> 00:18:26,382
THESE BOYS THAT, LIKE, COME
TO YOUR HOUSE AND COOK

517
00:18:26,382 --> 00:18:28,451
THIS FABULOUS,
LIKE, HEALTHY DISH.

518
00:18:28,451 --> 00:18:30,352
- YAY!
- Brian: ALL RIGHT, LADIES.

519
00:18:30,352 --> 00:18:31,720
BON APPETIT!

520
00:18:34,690 --> 00:18:36,125
Norelle: I SAID TODAY THAT--

521
00:18:36,125 --> 00:18:37,726
THAT I FEEL LIKE YOU HAVE
A WALL BUILT UP,

522
00:18:37,726 --> 00:18:38,994
BUT I UNDERSTAND
WHERE YOU'RE COMING FROM

523
00:18:38,994 --> 00:18:40,362
JUST BECAUSE THIS IS
A COMPETITION

524
00:18:40,362 --> 00:18:42,431
AND MAYBE THAT YOU DON'T WANNA
GET TOO CLOSE TO PEOPLE.

525
00:18:42,431 --> 00:18:43,833
Yaya: MAYBE IT IS A WALL.

526
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:47,102
YOU KNOW, WITH NINE BLOCKS
THAT SPELL OUT "COMPETITION."

527
00:18:47,102 --> 00:18:48,637
I'M LIKE, JUST
BECAUSE I KNOW

528
00:18:48,637 --> 00:18:50,239
THAT WE'RE ALL REACHING
FOR THE SAME GOAL.

529
00:18:50,239 --> 00:18:53,008
I DON'T HAVE A LOT OF
TOLERANCE FOR FAKENESS.

530
00:18:53,008 --> 00:18:56,645
YOU'RE THE ONE PERSON,
YOU KNOW, THAT I THINK IS--

531
00:18:56,645 --> 00:18:58,547
I CAN USE THE WORD "GROWTH."
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

532
00:18:58,547 --> 00:19:00,249
LIKE, I DON'T
HEAR YOU SPEAK THAT MUCH,

533
00:19:00,249 --> 00:19:02,718
BUT WHEN I HEAR YOU SPEAK,
YOU SAY PROFOUND THINGS.

534
00:19:02,718 --> 00:19:04,119
Norelle: WE UNDERSTOOD
WHERE WE'RE COMING FROM,

535
00:19:04,119 --> 00:19:05,588
WHICH I'M SO GLAD
THAT WE GOT TO DO,

536
00:19:05,588 --> 00:19:07,523
JUST BECAUSE I HAD
NOTHING OF YAYA,

537
00:19:07,523 --> 00:19:09,158
AND NOW I HAVE
A LITTLE SOMETHING.

538
00:19:09,158 --> 00:19:10,426
- THANK YOU.
- Yaya: OH.

539
00:19:12,294 --> 00:19:14,396
Ann: (gasps)

540
00:19:14,396 --> 00:19:16,732
"TOMORROW YOU WILL BE DRAPED
IN THE FINEST SILK IN THE WORLD.

541
00:19:16,732 --> 00:19:18,100
BE READY TO LEAVE AT 8
IN THE MORNING."

542
00:19:27,977 --> 00:19:30,312
- Jay: HELLO.
- Women: HELLO.

543
00:19:30,312 --> 00:19:33,282
Jay: SO THE COMPETITION
IS GETTING TOUGH.

544
00:19:33,282 --> 00:19:37,152
TODAY WE ARE GOING RIGHT
BACK IN TO BEAUTY SHOTS.

545
00:19:37,152 --> 00:19:38,654
BUT WE WANNA DO
SOMETHING ELSE,

546
00:19:38,654 --> 00:19:42,124
SO WE HAVE DIAMONDS TODAY.

547
00:19:42,124 --> 00:19:43,826
Women: YAY!

548
00:19:43,826 --> 00:19:46,962
Jay: YES, TODAY WE HAVE THE
VERRAGIO PLATINUM COLLECTION.

549
00:19:46,962 --> 00:19:49,265
SO I JUST WANT TO INTRODUCE YOU
TO THE PHOTOGRAPHER.

550
00:19:49,265 --> 00:19:51,367
HIS NAME IS BILL DIODATO.
COME OUT HERE, BILL.

551
00:19:51,367 --> 00:19:53,669
SO WHAT DO YOU THINK?
THEY'RE A PRETTY BUNCH.

552
00:19:53,669 --> 00:19:54,837
Bill: GORGEOUS.

553
00:19:54,837 --> 00:19:56,205
Jay: OKAY, COOL.
WE'LL START.

554
00:19:58,874 --> 00:20:00,442
Toccara: I'M READY TO GO.
I'M READY TO WORK THIS.

555
00:20:00,442 --> 00:20:03,946
THIS IS GONNA BE ABSOLUTELY
FABULOUS. F-A-B-O--

556
00:20:03,946 --> 00:20:05,014
Jay: IF I WERE YOU,
I'D BE IN THE MIRROR

557
00:20:05,014 --> 00:20:06,181
PRACTICING YOUR FACE
RIGHT NOW.

558
00:20:06,181 --> 00:20:07,283
Ann: I'M WAITING FOR MY HAIR.

559
00:20:07,283 --> 00:20:08,584
Jay: I WOULDN'T WORRY
ABOUT HAIR.

560
00:20:08,584 --> 00:20:10,953
I'D WORRY ABOUT GIVING
A BEAUTIFUL FACE. TRUST ME.

561
00:20:10,953 --> 00:20:12,288
Eva: I'M SO EXCITED.

562
00:20:12,288 --> 00:20:14,823
IT'S ACTUALLY EASIER
TO DO A BEAUTY SHOT, TO ME,

563
00:20:14,823 --> 00:20:17,293
BECAUSE IT'S LIKE, "HEY,
LOOK AT ME. IT'S MY FACE."

564
00:20:17,293 --> 00:20:18,394
IT'S SO EASY, YOU KNOW?

565
00:20:21,330 --> 00:20:22,631
Jay: SEE,
THAT'S REALLY PRETTY.

566
00:20:22,631 --> 00:20:24,400
OKAY, LET'S TAKE YOU
ON SET.

567
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:28,203
HEY, GUYS, I NEED TO TALK
TO ALL OF YOU AT ONCE.

568
00:20:28,203 --> 00:20:31,206
SO TO MAKE SURE THIS DOESN'T
LOOK LIKE A TYPICAL JEWELRY AD,

569
00:20:31,206 --> 00:20:33,609
WE DO HAVE SOMEONE ELSE FOR YOU
TO POSE WITH TODAY

570
00:20:33,609 --> 00:20:34,843
IN YOUR SHOT.

571
00:20:34,843 --> 00:20:36,879
SO CAN WE HAVE
OUR OTHER PERSON?

572
00:20:40,282 --> 00:20:41,951
Ann: YEAH!

573
00:20:41,951 --> 00:20:44,987
Eva: ARE WE POSING
WITH HER OR THE SPIDER?

574
00:20:44,987 --> 00:20:46,589
- Jay: THE TARANTULA.
- Ann: YES!

575
00:20:46,589 --> 00:20:48,190
Jay: THE TARANTULA'S
VERY SAFE,

576
00:20:48,190 --> 00:20:50,192
BUT WE DO HAVE
E.M.S. ON THE SIDE--

577
00:20:50,192 --> 00:20:51,460
Eva: WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
"IT'S VERY SAFE"?

578
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:52,795
WHY WOULD YOU HAVE TO
HAVE E.M.S. IF IT'S SAFE?

579
00:20:52,795 --> 00:20:54,797
Jay: WE HAVE E.M.S. HERE
ALL THE TIME.

580
00:20:54,797 --> 00:20:55,931
Eva: I DON'T LIKE SPIDERS.

581
00:20:55,931 --> 00:20:57,032
I DON'T WANT THEM
TO TOUCH ME.

582
00:20:57,032 --> 00:20:58,334
I DON'T WANT
TO BE NEAR THEM.

583
00:20:58,334 --> 00:21:00,269
IT'S A HORRIBLE PHOBIA
I'VE ALWAYS HAD.

584
00:21:00,269 --> 00:21:02,338
I'M REALLY IFFY RIGHT NOW.

585
00:21:10,345 --> 00:21:11,613
Jay: YOU READY, NICOLE?

586
00:21:11,613 --> 00:21:12,914
- Nicole: HE'S TICKLING ME.
- Bill: THAT'S GOOD.

587
00:21:12,914 --> 00:21:14,883
Eva: WHEN JAY SAID THERE WAS
GONNA BE A TARANTULA,

588
00:21:14,883 --> 00:21:18,486
I WAS SCARED.
IT'S PETRIFYING. IT'S SO SCARY.

589
00:21:18,486 --> 00:21:19,854
Ann: AAH!

590
00:21:19,854 --> 00:21:21,056
Jay: NO, NO, YOU GOTTA GO.

591
00:21:22,691 --> 00:21:25,660
Nicole: REALLY BADASS MISS EVA
COULDN'T HANDLE IT.

592
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:26,895
YOU KNOW, I DON'T THINK
SHE'S THE TOUGHEST

593
00:21:26,895 --> 00:21:28,697
AND BADDEST OF US ALL.
SHE'S JUST THE LOUDEST.

594
00:21:28,697 --> 00:21:30,598
Bill: RELAX.
KEEP YOUR EYES AT ME.

595
00:21:30,598 --> 00:21:33,168
I KNOW IT'S HARD RIGHT NOW.

596
00:21:33,168 --> 00:21:35,336
THAT'S PERFECT.
FLAWLESS.

597
00:21:35,336 --> 00:21:36,604
DON'T MOVE.

598
00:21:38,206 --> 00:21:39,641
FANTASTIC.

599
00:21:39,641 --> 00:21:41,776
Jay: NICOLE WAS REALLY
A PLEASURE TO SHOOT TODAY.

600
00:21:41,776 --> 00:21:43,545
50% OF HER FRAMES
WERE AMAZING,

601
00:21:43,545 --> 00:21:45,847
AND FOR ANY TOP MODEL,
THAT'S A FEAT.

602
00:21:45,847 --> 00:21:47,348
- Bill: GOT IT.
- Jay: OKAY, YEAH, WE GOT IT.

603
00:21:47,348 --> 00:21:48,683
Bill: FANTASTIC.

604
00:21:48,683 --> 00:21:51,086
Norelle: (inhales sharply)
Yaya: (inhales sharply)

605
00:21:51,086 --> 00:21:53,822
- Ann: IT'S NOT GONNA HURT.
- Toccara: OOH, IT MIGHT. OOH.

606
00:21:57,325 --> 00:21:59,394
Ann: A STUPID SPIDER
IS NOT GONNA STOP ME

607
00:21:59,394 --> 00:22:00,829
FROM, LIKE,
PURSUING MY DREAM.

608
00:22:00,829 --> 00:22:02,530
Eva: CAN WE TALK ABOUT
SOMETHING ELSE?

609
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,065
Ann: EVA IS,
LIKE, FLIPPING OUT

610
00:22:04,065 --> 00:22:05,567
LIKE A CHILD WOULD
THROW A FIT.

611
00:22:05,567 --> 00:22:08,536
HELLO, McFLY!
LIKE, STAY FOCUSED.

612
00:22:13,174 --> 00:22:14,476
♪ COME ON, FLASHIN' ♪

613
00:22:14,476 --> 00:22:16,010
♪ LACED WITH SHINY THINGS ♪

614
00:22:16,010 --> 00:22:17,045
♪ FLASHIN' ♪

615
00:22:17,045 --> 00:22:18,413
♪ GOLD AND DIAMOND RINGS ♪

616
00:22:18,413 --> 00:22:19,881
- ♪ FLASHIN'... ♪
- Bill: GORGEOUS.

617
00:22:19,881 --> 00:22:21,082
NICE WORK.

618
00:22:21,082 --> 00:22:23,351
THAT'S WHAT
WE'RE LOOKING FOR.

619
00:22:23,351 --> 00:22:25,220
Jay: YOU DEFINITELY HAVE
SOME REALLY GREAT OPTIONS.

620
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:28,189
Bill: RELAX THAT HAND.
RELAX THAT HAND.

621
00:22:28,189 --> 00:22:29,457
Yaya: DO I LOOK STIFF?

622
00:22:29,457 --> 00:22:30,992
Jay: I WANNA JUST TRY
SOMETHING THAT BRINGS

623
00:22:30,992 --> 00:22:32,460
A LITTLE MORE LIFE,
A LITTLE MORE MOVEMENT.

624
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:34,763
♪ FLASHIN' ♪
♪ LACED WITH SHINY THINGS ♪

625
00:22:34,763 --> 00:22:36,965
♪ FLASHIN' ♪
♪ GOLD AND DIAMOND RINGS ♪♪

626
00:22:36,965 --> 00:22:39,367
- Bill: FANTASTIC. DONE.
- Jay: WE GOT IT.

627
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:42,036
I LIKED THIS--
WHERE WE WERE GOING WITH THIS.

628
00:22:42,036 --> 00:22:44,639
OH, I LOVE THAT SHOT.

629
00:22:44,639 --> 00:22:45,907
Amanda: (squeals)

630
00:22:45,907 --> 00:22:48,643
SPIDERS, SPIDERS.
GET IT OFF.

631
00:22:48,643 --> 00:22:50,411
CAN I OPEN MY EYE
WITHOUT THE SPIDER CLAW

632
00:22:50,411 --> 00:22:52,013
GOING IN MY CORNEA?

633
00:22:52,013 --> 00:22:53,314
Jay: AMANDA,
IF YOU HOLD STILL,

634
00:22:53,314 --> 00:22:55,283
THE SPIDER WON'T PUT ITS FINGER
IN YOUR EYES,

635
00:22:55,283 --> 00:22:57,352
BUT YOU HAVE
TO OPEN THEM UP.

636
00:22:57,352 --> 00:22:59,254
Bill: I DON'T KNOW. I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO TELL YOU, JAY.

637
00:22:59,254 --> 00:23:00,822
I DON'T THINK THAT'S WORKING.

638
00:23:00,822 --> 00:23:03,525
Jay: A LITTLE LESS
FRIENDLY, AMANDA.

639
00:23:03,525 --> 00:23:05,560
IT'S GETTING A LITTLE
COMMERCIAL-LOOKIN'.

640
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:07,262
CLOSE YOUR MOUTH.

641
00:23:07,262 --> 00:23:09,697
YOU KNOW,
AMANDA STRUGGLED TODAY.

642
00:23:09,697 --> 00:23:13,968
UP THAT CLOSE, I DON'T KNOW
IF AMANDA IS A BEAUTY GIRL.

643
00:23:13,968 --> 00:23:16,504
Bill: I'VE BEEN
WAITING FOR THAT, YEAH.

644
00:23:16,504 --> 00:23:17,705
Jay: THANK YOU, AMANDA.

645
00:23:17,705 --> 00:23:18,973
Amanda:
OKAY, IT'S TANGLED.

646
00:23:20,074 --> 00:23:22,143
Jay: EVA'S ALREADY CRYING.

647
00:23:22,143 --> 00:23:24,813
YOU ALL RIGHT?

648
00:23:24,813 --> 00:23:27,482
Danilo: I THINK WE'LL ONLY
HAVE ONE SPIDER FATALITY TODAY.

649
00:23:27,482 --> 00:23:29,017
Jay: LET'S JUST HOPE
THE SPIDER DOESN'T THINK

650
00:23:29,017 --> 00:23:30,618
THE LASH IS HIS PARTNER.

651
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:31,820
Danilo: SHE HAS
A LOOK ON HER FACE

652
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:35,423
I'VE NEVER SEEN BEFORE TODAY--
PANIC-STRICKEN.

653
00:23:35,423 --> 00:23:38,026
- Eva: I'M SO SORRY, A.J.
- A.J.: THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

654
00:23:38,026 --> 00:23:41,296
Amanda: TO SEE HER CRYING
OVER SOMETHING LIKE A SPIDER

655
00:23:41,296 --> 00:23:46,234
MAKES DIVA EVA SEEM HUMAN.

656
00:23:52,607 --> 00:23:54,442
Bill: A LITTLE MORE ENERGY,
HON, LITTLE MORE ENERGY.

657
00:23:54,442 --> 00:23:56,578
Jay: SHE JUST DOES NOT
FEEL COMFORTABLE AT ALL.

658
00:23:56,578 --> 00:23:58,546
Bill:
I'M NOT SEEING ANYTHING.

659
00:23:58,546 --> 00:24:00,281
MORE. TURN TO ME. MORE.

660
00:24:00,281 --> 00:24:02,650
IF YOU WANNA BE AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL, YOU GOTTA FOCUS.

661
00:24:02,650 --> 00:24:05,053
Jay: NORELLE IS JUST NOT
COMFORTABLE WITH BEAUTY.

662
00:24:05,053 --> 00:24:08,389
SHE ONLY FEELS COMFORTABLE
WITH A FACE FULL OF MAKEUP

663
00:24:08,389 --> 00:24:11,392
AND A CAMERA PULLED OFF
FROM HER.

664
00:24:11,392 --> 00:24:12,627
Bill: DONE.

665
00:24:12,627 --> 00:24:14,429
MORE. GOOD. MORE, MORE.

666
00:24:14,429 --> 00:24:15,530
THIS WAY.

667
00:24:15,530 --> 00:24:17,932
Toccara: IT'S
THE ITSY-BITSY SPIDER.

668
00:24:19,367 --> 00:24:21,736
Bill: WIDE EYES.
BIGGER EYES, BIGGER EYES.

669
00:24:21,736 --> 00:24:23,838
YOU DON'T WANT 'EM
TOO BIG. GREAT.

670
00:24:25,607 --> 00:24:27,275
OKAY, OPEN YOUR EYES.

671
00:24:27,275 --> 00:24:28,877
RIGHT HERE AT ME.

672
00:24:28,877 --> 00:24:30,144
Bill: AND TOCCARA
HAD GREAT ENERGY,

673
00:24:30,144 --> 00:24:32,380
A DEFINITE SWEETHEART,
NOT A GREAT BEAUTY GIRL.

674
00:24:34,249 --> 00:24:35,383
THAT'S IT, LOVE.
YOU'RE DONE.

675
00:24:35,383 --> 00:24:36,851
THAT'S THE MOST FIERCE
THAT SHE'S LOOKED.

676
00:24:36,851 --> 00:24:38,586
- Jay: YOU LIKE THAT ONE?
- Yaya: LOOK AT THEIR FACES.

677
00:24:38,586 --> 00:24:41,422
GO READ. GO READ THEM.

678
00:24:41,422 --> 00:24:42,457
Jay: THAT'S IT.

679
00:24:42,457 --> 00:24:43,658
Bill: I MEAN,
I DID THE BEST I COULD.

680
00:24:45,627 --> 00:24:47,929
GREAT.
NOT TOO WIDE-EYED.

681
00:24:47,929 --> 00:24:49,564
A LITTLE MORE ALIVE.

682
00:24:49,564 --> 00:24:50,698
FOCUS, FOCUS. GREAT.

683
00:24:50,698 --> 00:24:52,500
LET'S BRING THAT SPIDER
DOWN A LITTLE BIT.

684
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:55,103
THERE'S NOT ENOUGH
BEHIND THE EYES.

685
00:24:55,103 --> 00:24:56,738
DON'T FORCE IT.
DON'T FORCE IT.

686
00:24:56,738 --> 00:24:59,574
Jay: ANN, HELP ME
HELP YOU OVERCOME THIS.

687
00:24:59,574 --> 00:25:01,576
LIKE, 'CAUSE I'M TOTALLY
AT A LOSS.

688
00:25:01,576 --> 00:25:05,647
THINK OF SOMETHING OTHER THAN
SITTING IN FRONT OF THAT CAMERA.

689
00:25:05,647 --> 00:25:07,315
Bill:
REAL ALIVE. GORGEOUS.

690
00:25:07,315 --> 00:25:09,117
Jay:
BILL, LOOK AT THIS.

691
00:25:09,117 --> 00:25:10,285
Bill: VERY GOOD.

692
00:25:10,285 --> 00:25:11,552
WHEN YOU GET THERE,
STAY THERE.

693
00:25:11,552 --> 00:25:13,354
- Jay: IT'S SO BEAUTIFUL.
- Bill: GORGEOUS EYES.

694
00:25:13,354 --> 00:25:15,156
FANTASTIC.

695
00:25:15,156 --> 00:25:18,026
AND WE SHOT 125 FRAMES,
AND YOU DON'T WANNA HAVE

696
00:25:18,026 --> 00:25:20,161
TO SHOOT THAT MANY FRAMES
TO GET THE SHOT.

697
00:25:20,161 --> 00:25:21,462
Jay: YEAH, WE'RE GOOD.

698
00:25:21,462 --> 00:25:24,399
SHE'S CONSISTENTLY FLAT
ON FILM.

699
00:25:24,399 --> 00:25:26,601
Bill: HOW ARE YOU, EVA,
WITH THE TARANTULA?

700
00:25:26,601 --> 00:25:27,635
HOW DO YOU FEEL ABOUT IT?

701
00:25:27,635 --> 00:25:29,570
Eva: LET'S JUST GET
THE FILM DONE.

702
00:25:29,570 --> 00:25:30,838
I'M DEATHLY AFRAID.

703
00:25:30,838 --> 00:25:33,641
Bill: SHE'S VERY, VERY
NERVOUS ABOUT THIS.

704
00:25:37,078 --> 00:25:39,013
Bill: CAN WE MOVE
THE SPIDER ONTO HER HAND?

705
00:25:39,013 --> 00:25:40,648
RELAX YOUR HAND
FOR A SECOND, LOVE.

706
00:25:40,648 --> 00:25:41,683
RELAX.

707
00:25:41,683 --> 00:25:42,850
LET'S GET SOME BLOOD
BACK IN THERE.

708
00:25:42,850 --> 00:25:43,885
Ann:
(whispers) SHE'S CRYING.

709
00:25:43,885 --> 00:25:45,553
Amanda: REALLY?

710
00:25:45,553 --> 00:25:47,355
Bill: CAN WE GET A TISSUE
FOR HER, PLEASE?

711
00:25:47,355 --> 00:25:49,324
Eva: SPIDER COMES OFF.
I JUST START CRYING.

712
00:25:49,324 --> 00:25:50,658
AND I WAS NOT FINISHED
WITH THE SHOOT.

713
00:25:50,658 --> 00:25:52,427
I WASN'T EVEN
HALFWAY DONE YET.

714
00:25:52,427 --> 00:25:54,228
Jay:
TEARS? LET ME FIX IT.

715
00:25:54,228 --> 00:25:55,730
LET ME FIX, LET ME FIX.

716
00:25:55,730 --> 00:25:58,232
CAN WE MOVE THE LIGHT
SO I CAN SEE HER FACE?

717
00:25:58,232 --> 00:25:59,334
Eva: I'M SO SORRY.

718
00:25:59,334 --> 00:26:00,468
Bill: PROBABLY ABOUT
FIVE MORE MINUTES,

719
00:26:00,468 --> 00:26:02,136
AND WE'LL BE DONE.

720
00:26:02,136 --> 00:26:03,237
Jay: YOU'RE COOL.

721
00:26:03,237 --> 00:26:05,907
ARE YOU READY TO SHOOT
A LITTLE MORE?

722
00:26:05,907 --> 00:26:07,275
YOU JUST KEEP THOSE THERE.

723
00:26:07,275 --> 00:26:08,643
- READY?
- Eva: MM-HMM. LET'S GO.

724
00:26:08,643 --> 00:26:10,011
Bill: STAY WITH ME
THE WHOLE TIME, OKAY?

725
00:26:10,011 --> 00:26:11,379
NO WORRIES ABOUT IT, OKAY?

726
00:26:11,379 --> 00:26:12,580
GORGEOUS.

727
00:26:12,580 --> 00:26:14,082
GETTIN' THIS. GORGEOUS.

728
00:26:14,082 --> 00:26:15,650
CAN YOU MOVE
THE SPIDER, PLEASE?

729
00:26:15,650 --> 00:26:18,019
Man: THIS IS WHAT IT TAKES
TO BE A PRO, HON.

730
00:26:18,019 --> 00:26:20,221
Bill: FANTASTIC.

731
00:26:20,221 --> 00:26:21,489
- Jay: HEY, BILL?
- Bill: YEAH.

732
00:26:21,489 --> 00:26:22,623
Jay: MIGHT AS WELL
TAKE HER OUT OF THAT TORTURE.

733
00:26:22,623 --> 00:26:24,559
Bill: SHE'S HAVING
A TOUGH TIME.

734
00:26:26,227 --> 00:26:28,563
Jay: SHE COULD GET
CUT 'CAUSE OF THIS.

735
00:26:28,563 --> 00:26:29,697
Yaya: COME WITH ME.

736
00:26:29,697 --> 00:26:30,732
Eva: I'M PROUD OF MYSELF
AT THE FACT

737
00:26:30,732 --> 00:26:32,734
THAT I GOT THROUGH IT.

738
00:26:35,370 --> 00:26:37,805
I'M DISAPPOINTED THAT
I SHOWED THE VULNERABILITY.

739
00:26:43,277 --> 00:26:44,445
Eva's mom:
How you doing?

740
00:26:44,445 --> 00:26:46,114
Eva:
OH, MOTHER, I HAD A DAY.

741
00:26:46,114 --> 00:26:50,418
I HAD TO DO A CHALLENGE
WITH A TARANTULA.

742
00:26:50,418 --> 00:26:52,887
- Eva's mom: (gasps)
- Eva: MOM, IT WAS HORRIBLE.

743
00:26:52,887 --> 00:26:54,489
Eva's mom: Oh, sweetie.

744
00:26:54,489 --> 00:26:55,757
Eva: I KNOW, AND I JUST--

745
00:26:55,757 --> 00:26:58,493
I DON'T WANNA GET SENT HOME
BECAUSE OF IT, YOU KNOW?

746
00:26:58,493 --> 00:27:01,863
Ann: HONESTLY, FOR AS HARD-ASS
AS EVA COMES OFF TO BE,

747
00:27:01,863 --> 00:27:03,364
I WAS REALLY SURPRISED
THAT SHE WAS CRYING

748
00:27:03,364 --> 00:27:04,899
SO MUCH ABOUT THE SPIDER.

749
00:27:04,899 --> 00:27:06,801
Eva: GETTING DOWN TO IT,
AND ANY MISTAKE YOU MAKE,

750
00:27:06,801 --> 00:27:09,103
YOU KNOW, COULD--
IT COULD BE THE END OF IT,

751
00:27:09,103 --> 00:27:10,104
AND I DON'T KNOW.

752
00:27:10,104 --> 00:27:11,773
IT'S JUST SO FRUSTRATING.

753
00:27:11,773 --> 00:27:13,408
Nicole:
EVA'S REALLY STRESSING.

754
00:27:13,408 --> 00:27:16,110
SHE'S WORRIED THAT HER
INABILITY TO PERFORM

755
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:18,246
WITH A SPIDER ON HER FACE
IS GONNA SEND HER HOME,

756
00:27:18,246 --> 00:27:19,914
SO I DON'T THINK THAT
SHE REALLY IS CUT OUT

757
00:27:19,914 --> 00:27:22,283
TO BE AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

758
00:27:22,283 --> 00:27:23,751
Eva: I ALLOWED IT
TO GET TO ME, YOU KNOW?

759
00:27:23,751 --> 00:27:25,553
'CAUSE I DON'T LET
NOTHING GET TO ME.

760
00:27:25,553 --> 00:27:28,523
I JUST FEEL LIKE
I LET MYSELF SLIP, YOU KNOW?

761
00:27:28,523 --> 00:27:30,191
I'M ACTUALLY VULNERABLE
AT THIS POINT.

762
00:27:30,191 --> 00:27:31,793
I MAY BE GOING HOME.

763
00:27:38,933 --> 00:27:40,701
Amanda: IT'S TYRA MAIL.

764
00:27:40,701 --> 00:27:42,537
"TOMORROW YOU MEET
WITH THE JUDGES."

765
00:27:42,537 --> 00:27:44,972
Eva: SOMEONE'S GOING HOME,
GUYS.

766
00:27:44,972 --> 00:27:47,375
Toccara: I THINK EVERYBODY IS
A LITTLE IFFY ABOUT TOMORROW,

767
00:27:47,375 --> 00:27:48,810
SO...

768
00:27:48,810 --> 00:27:51,145
I WAS REALLY A LITTLE DOWN,
YOU KNOW, DURING THE WEEK,

769
00:27:51,145 --> 00:27:53,681
BUT I'M STILL GONNA BE ME,
AND I'M STILL GONNA BE FABULOUS.

770
00:27:53,681 --> 00:27:56,184
I'M STILL GONNA GIVE
ALL THAT I HAVE.

771
00:27:56,184 --> 00:27:57,985
Eva: I HOPE
JAY'S NOT MAD AT ME.

772
00:27:57,985 --> 00:27:59,554
I WAS SUCH A PUNK.
I FEEL LIKE...

773
00:27:59,554 --> 00:28:01,622
I DON'T KNOW HOW MY PICTURES
ARE GONNA TURN OUT.

774
00:28:01,622 --> 00:28:02,790
I'M SO SORRY.

775
00:28:02,790 --> 00:28:04,225
I DON'T KNOW IF MY FEAR'S
GONNA PROJECT,

776
00:28:04,225 --> 00:28:07,128
AND IT'S JUST SO UPSETTING.
I JUST DON'T FEEL GOOD.

777
00:28:07,128 --> 00:28:08,796
Ann: LIKE, IT WAS SO STRANGE
'CAUSE HE CALLED ME OVER THERE.

778
00:28:08,796 --> 00:28:11,232
Jay: I'D WORRY ABOUT GIVING
A BEAUTIFUL FACE, TRUST ME.

779
00:28:11,232 --> 00:28:12,366
Ann: I THOUGHT HE WAS
GONNA CALL ME UGLY

780
00:28:12,366 --> 00:28:14,168
OR STUPID OR SOMETHING.

781
00:28:14,168 --> 00:28:16,003
I'M GOING TO BE
NERVOUS TONIGHT AT PANEL,

782
00:28:16,003 --> 00:28:17,972
JUST BECAUSE
IF I HAVE A BAD PICTURE,

783
00:28:17,972 --> 00:28:19,874
I FEEL LIKE I WILL BE
THE ONE GOING HOME.

784
00:28:30,284 --> 00:28:31,486
Tyra: HEY, GIRLS.

785
00:28:31,486 --> 00:28:32,687
Women: HELLO.

786
00:28:32,687 --> 00:28:34,789
Tyra: NOW IT'S TIME
TO MAKE OUR EIGHTH CUT,

787
00:28:34,789 --> 00:28:37,191
WHICH WILL BRING US
ONE STEP CLOSER

788
00:28:37,191 --> 00:28:41,062
TO FINDING OUT WHO WILL BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

789
00:28:41,062 --> 00:28:44,065
WE HAVE SOME AMAZING PRIZES--
A MODELING CONTRACT

790
00:28:44,065 --> 00:28:48,636
WITH THE TOP INTERNATIONAL
MODELING AGENCY, FORD MODELS,

791
00:28:48,636 --> 00:28:50,938
A PHOTO SPREAD
IN "ELLE" MAGAZINE,

792
00:28:50,938 --> 00:28:54,041
SHOT BY WORLD-RENOWNED
PHOTOGRAPHER GILLES BENSIMON,

793
00:28:54,041 --> 00:28:59,247
AND A $100,000 CONTRACT
WITH COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

794
00:28:59,247 --> 00:29:00,515
NOW IT'S TIME FOR ME
TO INTRODUCE

795
00:29:00,515 --> 00:29:03,718
OUR PANEL OF JUDGES--
JANICE DICKINSON.

796
00:29:03,718 --> 00:29:05,953
JANICE IS THE WORLD'S
FIRST SUPERMODEL EVER

797
00:29:05,953 --> 00:29:08,222
- TO EXIST ON THIS PLANET.
- Janice: FIRST.

798
00:29:08,222 --> 00:29:11,392
Tyra: NIGEL BARKER,
A NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER.

799
00:29:11,392 --> 00:29:14,896
NOLE MARIN, A PROMINENT FASHION
EDITOR AND STYLIST.

800
00:29:14,896 --> 00:29:17,798
WE HAVE OUR SPECIAL
GUEST JUDGE, REBECCA WEINBERG...

801
00:29:17,798 --> 00:29:19,233
Rebecca: GOOD TO SEE
YOU ALL AGAIN.

802
00:29:19,233 --> 00:29:22,703
Tyra: WHO IS A CELEBRITY
STYLIST EXTRAORDINAIRE.

803
00:29:22,703 --> 00:29:24,939
NOW IT'S TIME FOR YOUR
INDIVIDUAL EVALUATIONS,

804
00:29:24,939 --> 00:29:27,742
AND REBECCA IS GOING TO
ADMINISTER YOUR TEST.

805
00:29:27,742 --> 00:29:30,978
Rebecca: OKAY, GIRLS, HERE ARE
FIVE DIFFERENT OPTIONS OF HATS.

806
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:32,246
(laughter)

807
00:29:32,246 --> 00:29:34,282
Rebecca: YOU'RE GOING
TO PICK ONE OF THESE HATS.

808
00:29:34,282 --> 00:29:37,618
EACH ONE OF THEM REPRESENTING
A DIFFERENT STYLE.

809
00:29:37,618 --> 00:29:39,687
CHOOSE ONE, AND
YOU'LL HAVE TEN MINUTES

810
00:29:39,687 --> 00:29:43,057
TO BUILD YOUR IMAGE AROUND
YOUR HAT OF CHOICE.

811
00:29:43,057 --> 00:29:43,991
GO.

812
00:29:46,260 --> 00:29:47,528
♪ COME ON ♪♪

813
00:29:47,528 --> 00:29:50,531
♪♪♪

814
00:30:01,142 --> 00:30:02,543
Tyra:
FIRST, WE HAVE NICOLE.

815
00:30:03,911 --> 00:30:05,112
Janice: WHOO-HOO!

816
00:30:05,112 --> 00:30:06,647
Tyra: SO YOU CHOSE
THE MOTORCYCLE HAT

817
00:30:06,647 --> 00:30:09,183
AND THEN THREW ON
A TIARA, TOO.

818
00:30:09,183 --> 00:30:12,119
Nigel: YOU CAME OUT LIKE THIS,
I WAS LIKE, "WHOA. OKAY."

819
00:30:12,119 --> 00:30:13,187
Janice: YOU GOT SCARED.

820
00:30:13,187 --> 00:30:14,622
Nigel: I DID KINDA
GET SCARED.

821
00:30:14,622 --> 00:30:17,191
IT SEEMED ALMOST LIKE YOU WERE
PUTTING ON A BIT OF AN ACT.

822
00:30:17,191 --> 00:30:19,293
Rebecca: TOO FANTASY.
IT'S NOT FASHION.

823
00:30:19,293 --> 00:30:20,695
Tyra:
YOU HAD A PHOTO SHOOT.

824
00:30:20,695 --> 00:30:23,531
IT WAS FOR DIAMONDS,
AND YOU WERE ACCESSORIZED

825
00:30:23,531 --> 00:30:25,399
WITH A LIVE TARANTULA.

826
00:30:25,399 --> 00:30:26,667
Janice: UGH.

827
00:30:26,667 --> 00:30:28,402
Tyra: HERE IS
YOUR BEST SHOT.

828
00:30:28,402 --> 00:30:30,438
- Janice: THAT'S A LIVE BUG.
- Nigel: WOW.

829
00:30:30,438 --> 00:30:32,974
Nolé: THIS PHOTOGRAPH
DOESN'T LOOK ANYTHING LIKE YOU.

830
00:30:32,974 --> 00:30:34,008
YOU REALLY TRANSFORMED.

831
00:30:34,008 --> 00:30:35,209
Nigel: NO DOUBT
YOU'VE GOT THE POWER

832
00:30:35,209 --> 00:30:36,377
TO BE A GOOD BEAUTY MODEL.

833
00:30:36,377 --> 00:30:37,745
Janice: LOOKS MORE LIKE
AN ALBUM COVER.

834
00:30:37,745 --> 00:30:39,313
Tyra: YOU'RE RIGHT.
I SEE A RECORDING ARTIST,

835
00:30:39,313 --> 00:30:41,449
LIKE YOU SHOULD SING...
(dramatic voice) LIKE THIS. AHH.

836
00:30:41,449 --> 00:30:43,517
Janice: (laughs)

837
00:30:43,517 --> 00:30:44,652
Tyra: TOCCARA.

838
00:30:44,652 --> 00:30:46,654
Nigel: TOCCARA,
I DON'T REALLY UNDERSTAND.

839
00:30:46,654 --> 00:30:47,855
YOU LOOK LIKE YOU
DIDN'T DO ANYTHING

840
00:30:47,855 --> 00:30:49,123
OTHER THAN STICK A HAT
ON YOUR HEAD.

841
00:30:49,123 --> 00:30:51,158
Janice: SEE, YOU COULD
HAVE COME OUT AS TOCCARA,

842
00:30:51,158 --> 00:30:52,860
LIKE, "YEE-HAW, HONEY!"

843
00:30:52,860 --> 00:30:56,130
YOU KNOW, AND SHOWN US
THAT TOCCARA PERSONALITY.

844
00:30:56,130 --> 00:30:58,266
- ARE YOU WITH ME ON THIS?
- Toccara: I HEAR YOU.

845
00:30:58,266 --> 00:31:00,001
Janice: YOU HEAR ME,
BUT DO YOU UNDERSTAND?

846
00:31:00,001 --> 00:31:01,502
Toccara: I AGREE. I'M JUST
SOAKING IT IN.

847
00:31:01,502 --> 00:31:03,037
- I'LL TAKE IT.
- Janice: SHE'S TAKING IT.

848
00:31:03,037 --> 00:31:05,539
Tyra:
HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

849
00:31:05,539 --> 00:31:06,807
Janice: THE TARANTULA'S
TAKING OVER

850
00:31:06,807 --> 00:31:08,342
THE FACE AND THE JEWELRY.

851
00:31:08,342 --> 00:31:12,380
IT'S LIKE A BIG HAIRY MOLE--
A TARANTULA MOLE.

852
00:31:12,380 --> 00:31:13,914
Nolé: IT'S A GREAT SHOT
FOR THE SPIDER.

853
00:31:13,914 --> 00:31:15,249
Janice: YEAH.

854
00:31:15,249 --> 00:31:17,385
HOW'D YOU FEEL
WITH A LIVE TARANTULA

855
00:31:17,385 --> 00:31:19,320
WALKING ALL OVER YOUR
GORGEOUS FACE?

856
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:20,921
Toccara: IT WAS
A GREAT EXPERIENCE.

857
00:31:20,921 --> 00:31:22,189
- Janice: THAT'S IT?
- Tyra: WHERE ARE YOU?

858
00:31:22,189 --> 00:31:23,424
- Toccara: NO, I MEAN--
- Janice: PULL IT OUT!

859
00:31:23,424 --> 00:31:24,992
- WHAT THE HELL HAPPENED?
- Tyra: YOU'RE NOT HERE.

860
00:31:24,992 --> 00:31:27,295
Toccara: I AM HERE!
I HAD A GOOD TIME.

861
00:31:27,295 --> 00:31:28,763
- Tyra: SOMETHING'S WEIRD.
- Janice: YEAH.

862
00:31:28,763 --> 00:31:30,765
Tyra: YOU'VE CHECKED OUT.
HOW MANY TIMES HAVE I TOLD YOU

863
00:31:30,765 --> 00:31:32,133
YOU'RE VIVACIOUS,
YOU'RE GREAT?

864
00:31:32,133 --> 00:31:33,834
I WANNA SEE THAT,
AND WHEN YOU COME IN HERE,

865
00:31:33,834 --> 00:31:35,269
AND YOU'RE LIKE,
"THE PICTURE'S NICE.

866
00:31:35,269 --> 00:31:36,771
THE EXPERIENCE
WAS LOVELY."

867
00:31:36,771 --> 00:31:38,773
Nigel: YOU NEED TO INSTALL
THE PERSONALITY CHIP

868
00:31:38,773 --> 00:31:40,141
BACK INTO YOU.

869
00:31:40,141 --> 00:31:41,642
Toccara: OKAY.

870
00:31:41,642 --> 00:31:43,444
Tyra: NEXT WE HAVE AMANDA.

871
00:31:43,444 --> 00:31:45,246
Nolé: THIS IS
A DROP-DEAD LOOK.

872
00:31:45,246 --> 00:31:46,580
Nigel:
VERY ANNIE LENNOX.

873
00:31:46,580 --> 00:31:47,982
